<title>UK: UK Fergus oilfield produces first crude - Amerada.</title>
<headline>UK Fergus oilfield produces first crude - Amerada.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The North Sea Fergus oilfield produced its first oil on Monday, operator Amerada Hess Corp said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Fergus achieved an initial flow of 15,000 barrels per day after its development as a subsea tie-back to the Uisge Gorm floating production, storage and offloading vessel, located four miles northwest of the Fife field.</p>
<p>Developed in association with Premier Oil Plc, Fergus reserves are estimated at six million barrels.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
